From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: Test a dynamic image sampler's primary plane for null

STEAMAC-3W: release events fail Metal compilation at
is_null_texture(layerSampler) and is_null_texture(tex), where the helper
argument is spvDynamicImageSampler<float>, not a native Metal texture.
A YCbCr immutable sampler passed to a sampler2D helper enables this wrapper;
robustImageAccess2 then emits the invalid native null check.

Provide a matching overload next to the wrapper. The primary plane defines
whether the descriptor is null; absent extra planes are normal for one-
and two-plane images. Keep the null result at four zeros, including alpha.

The texture_helpers repro uses the same YCbCr/helper/robust-image path and
fails with the report's exact compiler error before this change.
---
diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -9631,6 +9631,14 @@ void CompilerMSL::emit_custom_functions()
 			end_scope();
 			end_scope_decl();
 			statement("");
+			// Robust image access tests combined image-sampler arguments just like native textures.
+			// The conversion's extra planes may legitimately be null; plane0 determines descriptor validity.
+			statement("template<typename T>");
+			statement("inline bool is_null_texture(spvDynamicImageSampler<T> image)");
+			begin_scope();
+			statement("return metal::is_null_texture(image.plane0);");
+			end_scope();
+			statement("");
 			break;
 
 		case SPVFuncImplRayQueryIntersectionParams:
